# Testing

| Library | Role |
| --- | --- |
| JUnit 4 | runner and assertions |
| MockK | repositories, `PasswordHasher`, other use cases |
| kotlinx-coroutines-test | `runTest` around `execute` |

Test use cases. That is where the rules are.

Do not test mappers. Do not test repository implementations. Do not test HTML or route wiring here.

Mock interfaces the use case receives. Build data classes with real constructors.

Repository methods block on JDBC. Stub them with `every`, not `coEvery`. `execute` is suspend, so the test still uses `runTest`.

One class, one file: `{ClassName}Test.kt`, same package under `src/test/kotlin`. Shared builders go in `util/`.

`Result` has `isSuccess`, `data`, and `error`. There is no `isError`.

```kotlin
@Test
fun `cycles an empty sticker to have`() = runTest {
    every { albums.loadSticker(userId, albumId, stickerId) } returns snapshot

    val result = useCase.execute(params)

    assertTrue(result.isSuccess)
    assertEquals("have", result.data.status)
}
```

Name the test for the behaviour: `` `returns email taken when the address is already used` ``. Not `testRegisterEmail`.

Arrange, act, assert. One behaviour per test.
